  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting access to clean and sustainable energy for a just transition in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a learning project with a key aim to understand the level access to energy by youth, women and indigenous communities and energy transition issues in Kenya and work towards setting the civil society agenda on the energy transition and climate change. The primary audience for this research is Oxfam as well as civil society, including partners of Oxfam, civil society actors, International Non -Governmental Organisation&apos;s (INGO&apos;s) and private sector actors working in the Energy Sector and towards lowering carbon emissions and cleaner transition.  The research will be carried out between May and June 2023 through a research consultancy and a sense making workshop in July 2023 with stakeholders mapped through the study working in the energy sector.</narrative>
  </description>
